.TH VC4D 8 "2026-11-20" "vc4-stack" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
vc4d \- VideoCore IV QPU helper daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B vc4d
[\fB\-\-socket\fR \fIPATH\fR] [\fB\-\-arena\-mb\fR \fIMB\fR]
[\fB\-\-group\fR \fIGROUP\fR] [\fB\-\-drop\-user\fR \fIUSER\fR]
[\fB\-\-max\-timeout\-ms\fR \fIMS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B vc4d
is the privileged half of the vc4-stack.  It opens
.I /dev/mem
once, maps the V3D register window, allocates the client arena from the CMA
heap, and then drops to an unprivileged uid with an empty capability set.
Clients talk to it over a Unix socket; they never open
.I /dev/mem
themselves.
.PP
The socket is created in
.I /run
with mode 0660 and group ownership of the group given by
.BR \-\-group .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-socket \fIPATH\fR
Unix socket to listen on (default \fI/run/vc4d.sock\fR).
.TP
.B \-\-arena\-mb \fIMB\fR
Size of the single shared client arena, in MiB (default 96).  The
vc4-toolkit-fast drop-in raises this to 150 for the 320x320 YOLO recipe.
.TP
.B \-\-group \fIGROUP\fR
Group that may connect to the socket (default \fIvc4\fR).
.TP
.B \-\-drop\-user \fIUSER\fR
User the daemon switches to after setup (default \fInobody\fR).
.TP
.B \-\-max\-timeout\-ms \fIMS\fR
How long one launch may run before the daemon declares the GPU wedged
(default 10000).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/default/vc4d
Defaults for the systemd unit (\fBVC4D_ARGS\fR).
.TP
.I /run/vc4d.sock
Client socket.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR vc4-query (1),
.BR vc4-smi (1),
.BR vc4infer (1)
